````markdown
# Version 6.2: Secure Vault and institution approval (28 October 2026)

Adds the screenshot features that were not in the repository, built with the v6.1 fixes in place.

## Institution approval by the regulator
- Self-registered institutions start as **PENDING** (`users.approval_status`). Until approved they see no student
  records and cannot register students, issue credentials, re-verify or run the tamper test — enforced on the server
  (`institutionIsActive` in `accessRules.ts`) and on screen (amber "Awaiting regulator approval" banner).
- Regulator gets an approval panel on the Audit page: `GET /api/admin/institutions`,
  `POST /api/admin/institutions/:uid/decision` (APPROVE / REJECT). Decisions are logged as
  `INSTITUTION_APPROVED` / `INSTITUTION_REJECTED`, and the institution unlocks live without signing in again.
- Demo: `coe@nitt.example.edu` (NIT Tiruchirappalli) is seeded as pending; the regulator demo account can approve it.

## APAAR Secure Vault
- **Institutions issue signed credentials** (`POST /api/db/students/:apaarId/credentials`), optionally with the PDF.
  The PDF's SHA-256 is part of the HMAC-signed payload, so swapping the file breaks the signature. Logged as `CREDENTIAL_SEALED`.
- **Students add their own copies** (`POST /api/db/me/documents`). These are fingerprinted but marked
  **"not issuer-verified"**: they are never counted as verified, never shown to employers and skipped by employer
  verification. Logged as `DOCUMENT_UPLOADED`.
- **File checks** (browser first, server decides, `src/utils/vaultRules.ts` + `src/server/uploads.ts`): real PDF header
  `%PDF-` and `%%EOF` trailer, 1 KB–5 MB, safe file name. The 279-byte file from the screenshot and renamed images are rejected.
- Counts come from one list everywhere: vault tab, header ("6 Documents · 5 issuer-signed · 1 your uploads") and
  Doc Verify ("Issuer-signed verified 5 of 5 + 1 student upload").
- Certificate view shows the real method (HMAC-SHA256 server key / SHA-256 only for self-uploads) instead of "X.509 / NAD Root CA".

## Verified
- 77 unit tests pass (new: upload validation, institution approval, employer never sees self-uploads).
- Browser: 17-step vault/approval flow, 26 role checks and the 7-step consent flow all pass against a live server + PostgreSQL.

